---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="45–55 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 14</p>
  <h1>Food &amp; <em>drink</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Choose the language frame that fits the serving you mean. Compare <span class="ex">some coffee</span>, <span class="ex">a coffee</span>, and <span class="ex">a cup of coffee</span>. Then use natural U.S. English to state a preference, place an order, check availability, and choose <span class="ex">for here</span> or <span class="ex">to go</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">45–55 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">countable views and amount views</span>
    <span class="tag">portions · orders · some / any</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min optional listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare items, amounts, and servings.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Choose a frame from the intended meaning.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Use portions and complete service exchanges.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Run a fictional lunch-counter role-play.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Meal words often form article-free routine chunks: <span class="ex">have breakfast</span>, <span class="ex">have lunch</span>, and <span class="ex">have dinner</span>. People eat at different times and may use different meal names, so these are language chunks, not a required daily schedule.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a role pattern, a clock phrase, and an article chosen from the first sound.">
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="as">as</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="for">for</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="half past">half past</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quarter to">quarter to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The profile labels Luis’s role “cook”: Luis works <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="as" data-hint="As introduces a person’s role." data-fix="Luis works as a cook." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a cook. <span class="contraction">(jobs and workplaces)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The lunch card shows 12:30: Lunch is at <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="half past" data-hint="Thirty minutes after twelve is half past twelve." data-fix="Lunch is at half past twelve." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> twelve. <span class="contraction">(telling the time)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The staff card gives Mina’s role: Mina is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Accountant begins with a vowel sound, so use an." data-fix="Mina is an accountant." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> accountant. <span class="contraction">(a or an)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the food and drink</h2>
