  <h2>Some and any in a food-service context</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Choose from the speaker’s meaning, not punctuation alone. <span class="ex">Some</span> can present an existing amount, an expected offer, or a requested amount. <span class="ex">Any</span> keeps a neutral inventory question open or contributes zero quantity after a negative.</p>
  <p><span class="ex">There is some soup. · Is there any soup? · There isn’t any soup. · Would you like some soup? · Can I have some soup?</span></p>
  <p>Match the verb to the noun frame: <span class="ex">There is some rice</span> but <span class="ex">There are two sandwiches</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You selected some or any from existing, open, zero, offer, request, and plural-quantity meanings.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose some or any from the stated situation</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Some or any choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="some">some</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="any">any</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The inventory card confirms bread is on the table: There is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-hint="The card confirms an existing amount, so present it with some." data-fix="There is some bread on the table." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> bread on the table.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The server has not checked the refrigerator yet: Is there <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="any" data-hint="A neutral inventory question with an open answer uses any." data-fix="Is there any milk in the refrigerator?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> milk in the refrigerator?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The sold-out sign confirms zero juice: We don’t have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="any" data-hint="After the negative don’t have, any contributes zero quantity." data-fix="We don’t have any juice today." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> juice today.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The server presents fruit that is available: Would you like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-hint="The offer presents fruit as available, so use some." data-fix="Would you like some fruit?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> fruit?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The customer requests an amount from the pitcher: Can I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-hint="A request for an amount commonly uses some." data-fix="Can I have some water, please?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> water, please?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The receipt confirms several countable items: We ordered <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="some" data-hint="The receipt confirms an existing plural quantity, so use some." data-fix="We ordered some sandwiches." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sandwiches.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

