  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="like" data-hint="The customer is ordering one coffee now, not describing a general preference." data-fix="I’d like a coffee, please." data-why="I like states a general preference. I’d like, meaning I would like, makes a polite present request.">
    <h3>Drill 5: preference or present order?</h3>
    <p>The customer is at the counter ordering now: “I like a coffee, please.” Tap the word that needs the contraction <span class="ex">’d</span> before it.</p>
    <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="like">like</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">a</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="coffee">coffee, please.</button></div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="breads" data-hint="The ticket requests two individual pieces, so count the unit piece rather than bread." data-fix="The order needs two pieces of bread." data-why="Bread is an amount noun in this meaning. To count individual parts, pluralize the unit: two pieces of bread.">
