  <h2>Use it safely and flexibly</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real diet, meals, health, allergies, religion, finances, shopping, refrigerator, home, or body. Use the fictional menu and order cards, invent details, or share personal preferences only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Menu viewpoint:</b> The fictional menu has sandwiches, soup, cake, coffee, and water. Present each as an item, amount, or portion: <span class="ex">a sandwich · a bowl of soup · a slice of cake · a cup of coffee · a bottle of water</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Preference and request:</b> Choose one fictional drink. First state a general preference with <span class="ex">I like</span>. Then place one current order with <span class="ex">I’d like</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Offer and response:</b> The server offers fruit, soup, or coffee. Accept one with <span class="ex">Yes, please</span> and decline another with <span class="ex">No, thank you</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Inventory change:</b> A sold-out card removes one item. Ask a neutral <span class="ex">any</span> question, give a zero-quantity answer, and offer an available alternative with <span class="ex">some</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: run a fictional lunch-counter exchange for 45–60 seconds.</b> Include a greeting, one countable item, one portion or container, one <span class="ex">some/any</span> exchange, an offer and response, <span class="ex">for here or to go</span>, and a polite close.</div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “A food noun can show one item, an ______, or a measured ______. <span class="ex">I like</span> states a general ______, but <span class="ex">I’d like</span> makes a present polite ______.”</p>
    <p>Then explain the difference between <span class="ex">some coffee</span>, <span class="ex">a coffee</span>, and <span class="ex">a cup of coffee</span>, and answer <span class="ex">For here or to go?</span> in two ways.</p>
  </div>

